# Cargo build artifacts — the vendored .wasm blobs live under
# ../bytecode/ (committed to git per Q9 + AMEND-A1); the per-scenario
# Cargo.toml + src/lib.rs are committed for operator-reproducibility
# per Task 20 PLAN, but the per-crate target/ + Cargo.lock are NOT
# checked in.
#
# EXCEPTION (phase 82): l_httpcall_success/Cargo.lock IS checked in. That
# blob is byte-reproducible ONLY under rustc 1.94.0 + log 0.4.30, and the
# `log` version is a TRANSITIVE dep of proxy-wasm =0.4.x — nothing in
# Cargo.toml pins it, so without the lock the blob silently drifts (log
# 0.4.33 yields a SAME-SIZE, 49791-bytes-different blob). The exception is
# deliberately NARROW: the other 13 scenario crates stay ignored so a
# build-all-14 run does not litter the worktree with untracked lock files.
target/
Cargo.lock
!l_httpcall_success/Cargo.lock
